WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.944
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:08.514
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.814 --> 00:00:14.961
Unit twenty-two: Protecting Heritage. Today you will say what must happen with passive modals.

4
00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:17.739
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.991
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:23.944
Heritage.

7
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.809
Heritage means traditions and places from the past.

8
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:30.509
Angkor Wat is part of our heritage.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.618
Your turn. Say: Heritage.

10
00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:37.456
Heritage.

11
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:39.264
Monument.

12
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.329
Monument means an old, important building or statue.

13
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:46.067
The monument is a thousand years old.

14
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.254
Your turn. Say: Monument.

15
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.275
Monument.

16
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:54.960
Preserve.

17
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.600
Preserve means to keep something safe from damage.

18
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.253
We must preserve old temples.

19
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.340
Your turn. Say: Preserve.

20
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:07.969
Preserve.

21
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:09.845
Restoration.

22
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.278
Restoration means repairing something to its first condition.

23
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:16.953
The restoration took ten years.

24
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.109
Your turn. Say: Restoration.

25
00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:24.293
Restoration.

26
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.051
UNESCO.

27
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:31.325
UNESCO means the United Nations group for education, science and culture.

28
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.473
UNESCO lists World Heritage Sites.

29
00:01:35.083 --> 00:01:37.399
Your turn. Say: UNESCO.

30
00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.304
UNESCO.

31
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.016
Tourism.

32
00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:46.957
Tourism means travelling and visiting places for fun.

33
00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.805
Tourism brings jobs to Siem Reap.

34
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:52.825
Your turn. Say: Tourism.

35
00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:56.552
Tourism.

36
00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.086
Culture.

37
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:02.290
Culture means the beliefs, art and customs of a people.

38
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:05.510
Apsara dance is part of Khmer culture.

39
00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:08.456
Your turn. Say: Culture.

40
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.173
Culture.

41
00:02:12.917 --> 00:02:14.452
Future generations.

42
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.669
Future generations means people who will live after us.

43
00:02:19.283 --> 00:02:22.003
Temples must be kept for future generations.

44
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:25.408
Your turn. Say: Future generations.

45
00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:29.860
Future generations.

46
00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:34.120
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:34.983 --> 00:02:37.575
Visal, why are heritage sites so important?

48
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:42.810
They show our history. Temples must be protected for the future.

49
00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:45.127
What should be done?

50
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:50.399
Old stones should be repaired carefully by experts.

51
00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:52.554
And tourists?

52
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:58.311
Rules must be followed. Walls mustn't be touched or climbed.

53
00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:00.851
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:05.446
Grammar focus: Passive with modals (must be protected).

55
00:03:05.746 --> 00:03:06.956
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.859
Temples must be protected for the future.

57
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.842
Monuments should be repaired carefully.

58
00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.854
Old carvings mustn't be touched.

59
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.969
After a modal, the passive is 'be' + past participle: must be protected, can be visited.

60
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:26.275
Be careful! Don't say: Temples must protected.

61
00:03:28.233 --> 00:03:30.662
Say: Temples must be protected.

62
00:03:30.962 --> 00:03:34.866
After a modal, the passive needs 'be' + past participle.

63
00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.400
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.561
Guarding the Past.

65
00:03:40.861 --> 00:03:44.347
Cambodia's heritage includes amazing temples and monuments.

66
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.646
Many sites are listed by UNESCO.

67
00:03:48.633 --> 00:03:51.759
Tourism helps, but heritage must be protected from damage.

68
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.532
Careful restoration should be done by experts.

69
00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:59.636
Our culture must be preserved for future generations.

70
00:04:00.733 --> 00:04:04.549
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.383 --> 00:04:06.860
Temples must be blank.

72
00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:11.185
A, protected. B, protect. C, protecting.

73
00:04:14.733 --> 00:04:16.930
The answer is A: protected.

74
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:20.942
Repairing something to its first condition is blank.

75
00:04:21.242 --> 00:04:25.000
A, restoration. B, tourism. C, heritage.

76
00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:30.997
The answer is A: restoration.

77
00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.533
People who will live after us are future blank.

78
00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:38.916
A, generations. B, monuments. C, tourists.

79
00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:45.349
The answer is A: generations.

80
00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:49.917
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:50.783 --> 00:04:53.027
Why should we preserve heritage sites?

82
00:05:01.817 --> 00:05:03.375
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:03.675 --> 00:05:13.247
We should preserve them because they tell our story. If they are damaged, they can never be replaced, so they must be protected for future generations.

84
00:05:13.547 --> 00:05:15.291
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:16.183 --> 00:05:21.123
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive with modals (must be protected).

86
00:05:21.423 --> 00:05:26.223
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

87
00:05:26.523 --> 00:05:30.232
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

88
00:05:30.532 --> 00:05:33.382
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

